{% set sw = spaceweather %}
{% set m = sw.metrics if sw else false %}

{# Staleness suffix for a metric, in words — never color. #}
{% macro note(x) %}
{%- if x.unavailable -%}
{%- elif x.expired %} <span class="stale-note">(feed interrupted; last reading {{ x.time_tag | utcTime }})</span>
{%- elif x.stale %} <span class="stale-note">(as of {{ x.time_tag | utcTime }}, older than usual)</span>
{%- endif -%}
{% endmacro %}

<h1>Space weather and propagation</h1>

{% if not m or sw.fetch_meta.total_outage %}

<p class="banner">Space-weather data is currently unavailable. NOAA's live
dashboards are at
<a href="https://www.spaceweather.gov/">spaceweather.gov</a>.</p>

{% else %}

<p class="provenance">Conditions for amateur radio, read from NOAA data.
Generated <time datetime="{{ sw.fetch_meta.generated_at }}">{{ sw.fetch_meta.generated_at | utcStamp }}</time>;
this page rebuilds about every three hours. For live graphics — including
color maps and the aurora oval — see NOAA's
<a href="https://www.spaceweather.gov/">spaceweather.gov</a>. Everything
here is also available as
<a href="/propagation.txt">plain text</a> and
<a href="/propagation.json">JSON</a>. New to these numbers?
<a href="#reading">Start at the bottom.</a></p>

